        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-12T17:01:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Does this need to be board specific code?  The devicetree already has the `active-mask` property.  Can the common motionsense code handle disabling and enabling the interrupt?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 20,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 20,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "baed890fa69e68321483d9146ad5cf9c0becdb7d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "33e41b08_9b7f31ed",
        "filename": "zephyr/program/fatcat/ruby-ish/src/sensor.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 20,
      "author": {
        "id": 1116125
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-13T17:14:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "At first I was thinking of a generic fix. \nThis requires a new driver quiesce op plus active-\u003einactive transition handling in sensor driver.\n\nA generic teardown placed in the deferred inactive branch of `motion_sense_switch_sensor_rate()` would race with an in-flight tcs3400_read() (no per-chip mutex serializes them).\nA race-free fix must run in the motion_sense task context, I think added here an \"else\" branch for inactive case. https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/common/motion_sense.c;drc\u003d14fbd2b99aca1d92cc15f3e9bfbbb520bb4d0460;l\u003d965.\n\nThis approach means more framework change. This issue happens to ISH while not EC. There are a few projects using EC ALS sensor. Current board-level fix only affects Ruby, however new project use inactive in S3 sensor have to implement the same in board level.\nI can propose a generic fix if we want this direction.",
      "parentUuid": "227aa619_eef49ef9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 20,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 20,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "baed890fa69e68321483d9146ad5cf9c0becdb7d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "87aa442b_8aa4e28c",
        "filename": "zephyr/program/fatcat/ruby-ish/src/sensor.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 20,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-13T23:17:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this same bug could affect the EC.  If the sensor generates an interrupt that is never serviced, the EC won\u0027t ever enter it\u0027s sleep mode while the overall system will stay in S0ix.  This can cause the EC power consumption to increase, but likely by a smaller amount than the ISH blocking S0i2.0 residency.\n\nI\u0027d like to see a proposal for how this could be incorporated in the motionse_sense task.  I\u0027m thinking a new devicetree property could be used to mark sensors that need some special handling regarding their interrupt.\n\nThe proposal doesn\u0027t need to be a working implementation, just an outline of how it might work.",
      "parentUuid": "33e41b08_9b7f31ed",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 20,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 20,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "baed890fa69e68321483d9146ad5cf9c0becdb7d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e583a339_adb97ee5",
        "filename": "zephyr/program/fatcat/ruby-ish/src/sensor.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 20,
      "author": {
        "id": 1116125
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-14T22:29:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "dts is a good idea. The change would be:\n1. Add new property: devicetree boolean `int-disable-on-inactive`\n\n2. project\u0027s motion sensor node which need to disable int pin during inactive, add properties:\n`int-disable-on-inactive`\n`int-signal`\n(this is existing property, seems not used in any project)\n\n3. In `motion_sense_switch_sensor_rate()` which is called by suspend/resume hook in motion_sense.c: \non the inactive branch call `gpio_disable_interrupt(int_signal); `\non the active branch (after `motion_sense_init`) call `gpio_enable_interrupt(int_signal)`.",
      "parentUuid": "87aa442b_8aa4e28c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 20,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 20,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "baed890fa69e68321483d9146ad5cf9c0becdb7d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "17702977_705b019d",
        "filename": "zephyr/program/fatcat/ruby-ish/src/sensor.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 20,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-18T13:49:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree that int-signal is not used.  All the handling regarding that property is dead code.  If you assigned `int-signal` on a board, I expect you would get a compile error.\nSpecifying both the `int-disable-on-inactive` and the interrupt in the devicetree is a good approach.  But you should call the interrupt signal `irq-gpios` to follow the Zephyr convention, and pass this directly to `gpio_disable_dt_interrupt` and `gpio_enable_dt_interrupt` in the switch sensor rate code.\n\nThis approach will allow us to also deprecate the [`sensor-irqs`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/dts/bindings/motionsense/cros-ec,motionsense-sensor-info.yaml;drc\u003dd7bf18325e3424fe98bbb454c3f25b741b920ca1) property.  We can then migrate platforms to the `irq-gpios` property and then eventually delete all the [sensor-irqs support code](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/shim/src/motionsense_sensors.c;l\u003d401;drc\u003d9c051f850d2de02f78451f525c44ec74215f4b36).\n\nIn the short term, you can add some build assert checks to verify that both `sensor-base-\u003eirq-gpios` and `sensor-info-\u003esensor-irqs` are not enabled at the same time.",
      "parentUuid": "e583a339_adb97ee5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 20,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 20,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "baed890fa69e68321483d9146ad5cf9c0becdb7d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
